From: MedyMa <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6.6 v3] net: sfp: warm-reboot recovery via TX_DISABLE + I2C recovery

On warm reboot SFP modules stay powered, potentially leaving the
I2C state machine stuck.  Pulse TX_DISABLE 300 ms + settle 500 ms,
retry 3×, then recover I2C bus.  Also triggers on cold boot with
module inserted — the recovery is a no-op on a clean bus.

v3: GPIO_MODDEF0 / GPIO_TX_DISABLE enum constants, dev_warn→dev_err.
v2: 300 ms pulse, 500 ms settle, 3 retries, I2C recovery.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -3348,4 +3348,36 @@ static int sfp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Warm-boot recovery: pulse TX_DISABLE + I2C recovery to reset
+	 * a potentially stuck I2C state machine.  Also triggers on cold
+	 * boot with module inserted (harmless no-op on clean bus).
+	 */
+	if (sfp->gpio[GPIO_MODDEF0] && !IS_ERR(sfp->gpio[GPIO_MODDEF0]) &&
+	    gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[GPIO_MODDEF0])) {
+		int retry;
+
+		if (sfp->gpio[GPIO_TX_DISABLE] &&
+		    !IS_ERR(sfp->gpio[GPIO_TX_DISABLE])) {
+			for (retry = 0; retry < 3; retry++) {
+				dev_info(sfp->dev,
+					 "warm boot: TX_DISABLE pulse %d/3\n",
+					 retry + 1);
+				gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[GPIO_TX_DISABLE], 1);
+				msleep(300);
+				gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[GPIO_TX_DISABLE], 0);
+				msleep(500);
+
+				if (gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[GPIO_MODDEF0]))
+					break;
+			}
+		}
+
+		if (sfp->i2c)
+			i2c_recover_bus(sfp->i2c);
+
+		if (!gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[GPIO_MODDEF0]))
+			dev_err(sfp->dev,
+				"warm boot: module not responding after reset\n");
+	}
+
 	if (sfp->need_poll)
